# J13 — Deep view tour (broad, shallow — run AFTER the deep journeys)
# Cycle every verb-reachable ShellView, capturing each. Judge: top-bar /
# footer / status chrome stays truthful per view.
name: Deep view tour (chrome truthfulness sweep)
env: KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
wait-for: 30 kuzushi>
submit: modules
wait: 2
snap: view-catalog
submit: tools
wait: 2
snap: view-tools
submit: options
wait: 2
snap: view-options
submit: config
wait: 2
snap: view-config
submit: workspace
wait: 2
snap: view-workspace
submit: context
wait: 2
snap: view-context
submit: kb
wait: 2
snap: view-knowledgebase
submit: tasks
wait: 2
snap: view-tasks
submit: findings
wait: 2
snap: view-findings
submit: activity
wait: 2
snap: view-activity
submit: jobs
wait: 2
snap: view-jobs
submit: history
wait: 2
snap: view-history
submit: story
wait: 2
snap: view-story
submit: help
wait: 2
snap: view-help
ask: Sweep the captures — does the top bar / footer / status chrome stay truthful on every view (mode label matches the view, keybind hints actually work there, no stale LIVE/phase chips)?
